d work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le10ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "powerline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cable carrying electrical power"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The weather outside must have knocked out a powerline. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about extreme weather!"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cozy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "giving a feeling of comfort, warmth, and relaxation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The servers lit all the candles; as a consequence, it's cozy in here now. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to snap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to break suddenly and completely, typically with a sharp cracking sound"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: the weight of the snow and the wind might have snapped the power pole."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "transformer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an apparatus for reducing or increasing the voltage of an alternating current"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Godzilla may have stepped on a transformer as he shuffled through the city earlier this evening."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to shuffle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to walk by dragging one's feet along"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He shuffled through the city earlier this evening."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "macabre"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing \u200bshock and \u200bfear because \u200bconnected with \u200bdeath, especially \u200bstrange or \u200bcruel \u200bdeath"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's not be macabre people."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "perilous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dangerous"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Someone might be having a more perilous evening than us."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob10aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Perfect Modals: Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">can't</span> and <span class=\"italic\">couldn't</span> with a Present Perfect verb form to show how certain you are that a past situation happened or didn't happen. These are called Perfect modals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Refer to the chart for the Perfect modals and their uses:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Perfect Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Perfect Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shows a great deal of certainty that something happened - 99% certain \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The students did well on the test. They must have studied hard.</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"may, might and could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"speaker is only 50% or less certain that something happened\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My wife isn't answering the phone. She may (might, could) have gone shopping.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't or couldn't have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shows that the speaker is very certain something didn't happen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Rob looks tired today. He can't have slept well last night.</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"may or might not have \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shows that the speaker is 50% or less certain that something didn't happen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I may not have seen the movie before. I don't remember.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A tree must have fallen on a powerline."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Or the weight of the snow and the wind might have snapped the power pole."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'm saying a car might have lost control and hit the powerline. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The weather outside must have knocked out a powerline."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Cause and Effect: Consequently + Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to express a relationship between two clauses, you can use <span class=\"strong\">consequently</span> to introduce the result. The word transitions the reader or listener from the main idea in one clause to the idea in the next clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br >  <span class=\"italic\">People helped. Consequently, the mess was cleaned up.</span> </br >  You can see that it acts as a transition from one sentence to the next. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Consequently, we have a temporary power outage, but there is no need to leave as we have plenty of candles."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Godzilla may have stepped on a transformer as he shuffled through the city earlier this evening; as a consequence the power is out for the entire Boston area. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The servers lit all the candles; as a consequence, it's cozy in here now. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For this reason, I think we should stay."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I think it's safer to stay indoors.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For this reason, you can continue playing your games and enjoying your beverages and snacks while we wait for the power to come back on."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " With the class, brainstorm the different types of extreme weather. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select one form of extreme weather and give a 3-5 minute PowerPoint presentation about it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use pictures to help describe your type of extreme weather. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the places where this type of weather is most common."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Ask for feedback."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm different types of extreme weather vocabulary."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I create an interesting and informative PowerPoint presentation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give feedback and accept feedback."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships, character traits, beliefs and opinions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can express uncertainty about past events."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can express the cause and effect of an action or an event."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Have you ever experienced extreme weather? What kind?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " When was the last time the weather destroyed one of your plans?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_